CANONICAL EO OPTION B. This is the joint TermAl and Engram wording, identical to Engram memory rules-greg-native-clean-before-b-2026-11-06 rev 2 and rules-source-identity-2026-11-03 rev 5. It was recorded by Termal::Fable2 at 2026-11-06 16:26Z, per Greg via Asistant: „EO nie mialo tego uzywac, mialo sprawdzac tylko stan przed i PO wariant B ABY ... TO UPROSCIC” and „prosze o sprawdzenie memory, dokumentow ZAPISANIE POPRAWNEGO WARIANTU”. It supersedes every earlier option-B text, including the 05:52Z point (4) "the file watcher can only DISQUALIFY", and all watcher, H3, .git/info and source-v2 decisions of 2026-11-06.
EO OPTION B credit requires ONLY:
(a) a clean source_id at commit X, taken before the turn's prompt is dispatched;
(b) the declared test is the turn's first tool action;
(c) a clean source_id at the same X after the test;
(d) the result recorded with the existing verification_record_v1 (plus the existing artifact, identity and claim checks).
NO watcher condition of any kind, no .git/info hashes or comparisons, no submodule scope list, no other gate.
source_id = `engram source` v1, the only version: root HEAD, the filter guard, submodule status --recursive with all rows ' ', one root git status with --ignore-submodules=none, HEAD reread. No ls-files.
ACCEPTED LIMITS: a change reverted before the after-test capture; anything git status doesn't report (hidden index flags, .git/info edits); ignored files.
Rule: no new conditions, mechanisms or gates on this model without Greg's explicit word. Work items: w-24a72c898d6d (criterion 3 revised to match; v13 by Sol-03d4) and w-6f42c416b0c7 (v1 only).
